course: dictionary
lesson: 14468
title: Taking part
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To participate means to take part in something, or to join in. When you join in a game, a club or a class activity, you participate. «Everyone can participate in sports day.» The clue is that everyone is invited to join in, so participate must mean take part.
explain: Look at the small word that comes after it. We say participate in something: «She participated in the science fair.» Participated is the past tense, so it already happened. Participates goes with he, she or it, and participating goes with words like «is» or «was».
explain: In school reports you might read, «He participates well in class discussions.» That means he joins in with the talking and sharing of ideas. Try swapping in join in: «He joins in well in class discussions.» If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
explain: A person who takes part is a participant, and taking part is called participation. «Active participation» means joining in with energy and effort. Clubs, games and projects all need participants.
fact: Participate means to take part in an activity or event, or to join in.
fact: Participate is a verb. Its forms are participate, participates, participated and participating.
fact: «Participation» is the noun for taking part, and «participant» is a person who takes part.
fact: «Participate fully» means taking part in every way you can. In formal writing, participate can also mean to share in something.
exercise: «Everyone can participate in sports day.» What does participate mean? | Sleep through it | Cancel it | *Take part and join in | Watch quietly from the side
exercise: Which word means a person who takes part? | Parties | Participle | Particle | *Participant
exercise: Choose the right form: «She ___ in the school play last year.» | participating | participate | participates | *participated
test: What does «active participation» mean? | Losing interest in the work | *Joining in with energy and effort | Being late for class | Sitting still and watching
test: Which word has the closest meaning to participate in a club? | Look at a map of the club | *Join in and take part | Sleep in the hall | Leave the club
exam: Which word completes this sentence? «Thank you for your ___ in the quiz.» | participate | participates | *participation | participant
